        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89">

                <pb facs="0253" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg119"/>

                <head>No. 89.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Hall.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-25"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 25,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 540.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information copies of
                    papers, under oath, in relation to the claim of Julius R. Schultz, under Title
                    LXXII of the Revised Statutes of the United States, as discoverer of guano
                    deposits on Vivorilla Key, off the coast of Honduras.</p>
                <p>I have explained in a letter to Mr. J. Gorham Moale, of Baltimore, of to-day’s
                    date, that the decision of the Department upon the claim of Mr. Schultz had been
                    deferred, owing to a question of sovereignty over the island, and promised to
                    acquaint him of the result of the Department’s investigation as soon as
                    practicable.</p>
                <p>Accordingly, I will thank you to ascertain whether Vivorilla Key is under the
                    dominion of the Government of Honduras, or other nation.</p>
                <p>In this connection reference is made to your No. 41, of December 14, 1882, upon
                    the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F.
                        Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d89-a1.xml" xpointer="d89-a1"/>
            </div>
